# Example requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Start the stack first: make up
@base = http://localhost:8080
@key = dev-key

### Send a batch of events (202, returns the ids)
POST {{base}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  {"id": "6f1d2c1a-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "type": "page_view", "user_id": "u-42", "payload": {"path": "/kampanyalar"}},
  {"id": "6f1d2c1a-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "type": "purchase", "user_id": "u-42", "payload": {"order": "o-1001", "total": 1499.9}}
]

### Read one back once a worker stored it (404 while it is still buffered)
GET {{base}}/v1/events/6f1d2c1a-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### Same ids again: accepted, but no duplicate rows
POST {{base}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

[{"id": "6f1d2c1a-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "type": "page_view", "user_id": "u-42"}]

### Validation error: 422 with the index of the bad event
POST {{base}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
Content-Type: application/json

[{"type": "click", "user_id": "u1"}, {"type": "", "user_id": "u1"}]

### Without an API key: 401
POST {{base}}/v1/events
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "click", "user_id": "u1"}

### Readiness (checks Postgres and Redis) and metrics
GET {{base}}/readyz

###
GET {{base}}/metrics
